WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:14.660
Last time: Sound → Words → Patterns

3
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.880
Chapter 3 · Chatting With Computers

4
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:29.590
How does a computer decide what to say?

5
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.500
Meet Anaya and her panda project

6
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:43.910
Anaya types: "What do pandas eat?"

7
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:51.550
Pip: "Pandas mostly eat bamboo!"

8
00:00:51.550 --> 00:01:01.830
How did Pip know? A tiny person inside?

9
00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:10.630
No person inside. Pip is a chatbot!

10
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.730
Chatbot = a program that chats by typing replies

11
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:23.060
Homework apps · Game help · Ticket apps

12
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:31.950
A program. Not a person, not magic.

13
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:40.520
Step 1: spot the key words · pandas · eat

14
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:49.890
It learned patterns from lots of examples

15
00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:57.130
Predict = a smart guess about what comes next

16
00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:06.610
Twinkle, twinkle, little ___?

17
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:16.460
Star! You predicted from a pattern.

18
00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:25.720
Chat tree: if the user says this, reply that

19
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:32.540
"I feel bored." → "Want a fun animal fact?"

20
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:44.570
Yes → octopus fact · No → a riddle

21
00:02:44.570 --> 00:03:08.320
"I feel bored." Which reply is best?

22
00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:17.770
A: it matches, and it's safe!

23
00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:27.290
Pip: "I'm your best friend!"

24
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:35.950
Does Pip really know her? Think!

25
00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:46.600
No feelings. Just predicting friendly words.

26
00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:56.210
Real friends are real people!

27
00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:07.940
Pip: "A spider has six legs." Right?

28
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:14.370
The book says eight legs! Pip was wrong.

29
00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:27.210
Predictions are guesses. They can be wrong.

30
00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.400
Check big facts with a grown-up or a book

31
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:39.570
Safe or unsafe to type?

32
00:04:39.570 --> 00:05:00.280
Which ones are safe to type?

33
00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:17.130
Questions & stories: safe. Private info: never!

34
00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:32.170
Chats can be saved. Ask a grown-up first!

35
00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:36.120
Your turn: practice check

36
00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:47.720
Tell a chatbot where the keys hide? Why?

37
00:05:47.720 --> 00:06:01.210
No! It's private, and chats can be saved.

38
00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:07.180
Chatbots predict replies from patterns

39
00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.550
Chatbots have no feelings

40
00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.750
They can be wrong. Check big facts!

41
00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:18.840
Never share secrets or private info

42
00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:24.130
Chapter 3 done!

43
00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:30.930
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
